When running `R.exe` or `Rterm.exe` version 4.5.1 using the usual Windows console host or the `mintty.exe` terminal from Rtools, pressing Ctrl+D offers to exit R ("Save workspace image? [y/n/c]:"). With Rterm.exe version 4.6.1, Ctrl+D causes R to prompt for continuation.

This is due to the fix for Bug 15941. In both R-4.5 and R >= 4.6, typing Ctrl+D at the beginnig of the line on Windows returns an empty string to the REPL. (`R_ReadConsole(...)` returns nonzero with `*state->buf == '\0'`.) Prior to R-4.6, this terminated R_ReplConsole due to the parser returning an EOF condition:

```
R_ReplConsole (rho=0x192f435e018, savestack=0, browselevel=0) at main.c:318
318             if(status < 0) {
(gdb) l
313         state.bufp = state.buf;
314         if(R_Verbose)
315             REprintf(" >R_ReplConsole(): before \"for(;;)\" {main.c}\n");
316         for(;;) {
317             status = Rf_ReplIteration(rho, savestack, browselevel, &state);
318             if(status < 0) {
319               if (state.status == PARSE_INCOMPLETE)
320                 error(_("unexpected end of input"));
321               return;
322             }
(gdb) p status
$21 = -1
(gdb) p state.status
$22 = PARSE_EOF
```

In R >= 4.6, when the parser is in the EOF state, the REPL keeps asking the console for more information:

```
#0  Rf_ReplIteration (rho=rho@entry=0x1b59b2ad298, savestack=savestack@entry=0,
    browselevel=browselevel@entry=0, state=state@entry=0x18769fe9f0) at main.c:296
296             R_IoBufferReadReset(&R_ConsoleIob);
(gdb) l 228
...
228         R_CurrentExpr = R_Parse1Buffer(&R_ConsoleIob, 0, &state->status);
229
230         switch(state->status) {
...
290         case PARSE_EOF:
291             /* the parser thinks it is EOF but it may not have seen all of the
292                input, so postpone the decision to exit until there is really
293                no more input (the parser may be seeing a sequence of spaces)
294                PR#15941 */
295         case PARSE_INCOMPLETE:
296             R_IoBufferReadReset(&R_ConsoleIob);
297             state->prompt_type = 2;
298             return(2);
299         }
(gdb) p state->status
$21 = PARSE_EOF
```

On Linux, pressing Ctrl+D makes `R_ReadConsole()` -> `Rstd_ReadConsole()` return 0 (because `readline` sets `rl_data.readline_eof`). `getline()` should return 1 (EOF) instead of 0 (success) when it sees a `^D` at the beginning of the input line, causing `R_ReadConsole()` to return 0 on Windows as well:

```
Index: src/gnuwin32/getline/getline.c
===================================================================
--- src/gnuwin32/getline/getline.c	(revision 90582)
+++ src/gnuwin32/getline/getline.c	(working copy)
@@ -781,7 +781,7 @@
 		    gl_buf[0] = 0;
 		    gl_cleanup();
 		    gl_putc('\n');
-		    return 0;
+		    return 1;
 		} else {
 		    gl_del(0);
 		}
```

(this passes `make check-devel` on Windows and doesn't touch any code paths on non-Windows)
